Route SM80 speculative verification on FlashInfer + static FP8 KV through the
split-KV Triton verifier, including mixed decode+prefill scheduler batches.

This patch is opt-in with VLLM_FP8_SPEC_VERIFY=1 and depends on:

  spec-decode-attn.patch
  spec-decode-int8-kv.patch
  spec-decode-fp8-kv-sm80.patch

Normal FlashInfer prefill and single-token decode are unchanged. The runtime
hook owns only the speculative decode slice, so trailing prefill rows still use
the normal path. It requires FP8 KV, no sliding window/softcap/alibi/sink, DCP
off, and NHD cache layout.

VLLM_FP8_SPEC_FULL_CG=1 is a second explicit qualification gate. On exact SM80
with E4M3 cache configuration (including uint8 physical storage created by the
heterogeneous-page layer), it advertises UNIFORM_BATCH graph support. Other
architectures, cache dtypes, and default launches retain upstream capability
reporting.

Written against vLLM 0.27.1. Apply with
experimental/cmp170hx-mixed-fp8/install.sh after the normal kernel patches.

